    {
      "id": "u2fDU8smV4Y54qCcLB_8M",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 907.8571526060412,
      "y": 1264.3522095116807,
      "width": 786.3995361328125,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0A",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 19749586,
      "version": 727,
      "versionNonce": 777793859,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782162506688,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "** How user can automatically sync files across devices\n-- When a user updates a file on their local machine, \nwe need to sync these changes with the remote server. \nWe consider the remote server to be the source of truth, \nso it's important that we get it consistent as soon as possible\nso that other local devices can know when there are changes they should pull in.\n-- To do this:\n1) monitor local Dropbox folder for changes in OS-specific file system events\n2) detects changes, queue the modified file for upload locally\n3) use our upload API to send the changes to server along with updated\nmetadata\n4) Conflicts ares resolved using \"last write wins\" strategy.\n-- 2 options:\n1) Polling:\n-- periodic polling GET /file/changes?since={timestamp} to \ncatch any change we might miss (if web socket drop)\n2) Web socket or SSE: -- change events through websocket\nThe server maintains an open connection with each client \nand pushes notifications when changes occur. \nThis is more complex but provides real-time updates.\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "** How user can automatically sync files across devices\n-- When a user updates a file on their local machine, \nwe need to sync these changes with the remote server. \nWe consider the remote server to be the source of truth, \nso it's important that we get it consistent as soon as possible\nso that other local devices can know when there are changes they should pull in.\n-- To do this:\n1) monitor local Dropbox folder for changes in OS-specific file system events\n2) detects changes, queue the modified file for upload locally\n3) use our upload API to send the changes to server along with updated\nmetadata\n4) Conflicts ares resolved using \"last write wins\" strategy.\n-- 2 options:\n1) Polling:\n-- periodic polling GET /file/changes?since={timestamp} to \ncatch any change we might miss (if web socket drop)\n2) Web socket or SSE: -- change events through websocket\nThe server maintains an open connection with each client \nand pushes notifications when changes occur. \nThis is more complex but provides real-time updates.\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "gCjSb298tLk0MX7LKM8WW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 421.5648970300616,
      "y": 1814.3325684462511,
      "width": 1010.71923828125,
      "height": 625,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0C",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1618226578,
      "version": 1424,
      "versionNonce": 430749805,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782162506688,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** Large file upload handle\n-- call use techique like chunking to break file into smaller pieces and upload independently\n-- chunking happen in client before it send to server\n-- user resume upload, we could check chunks field to see which chunk has been upload and which hasn't\n-- to keep chunks field in sync:\n---> can implement server-side verification of chunk uploads using ETags.\n---> can leverage S3 multipart upload\n--> verify these ETags by calling S3's ListParts API, \nproviding an efficient way to validate multiple chunks at once. \n\n--  Content-Defined Chunking (CDC), where chunk boundaries are determined by the file's content \nusing a rolling hash (like Rabin fingerprinting). With CDC, \na small edit only affects the chunks immediately surrounding the change, \nthe vast majority of chunks remain identical. \nThis is how systems like Dropbox actually achieve efficient delta sync in practice.\n-- Also can utilize compression to speed up upload/download. compression is only useful\nif speed gained from transferring fewer bytes outweight time it take to compress\nand decompress the file\n\n** Ensure file security\n-- ensure file are secure and only accessible to authorized users\n1. Generation: signURL on server, include URL path, expiration timestamp,\nrestriction (IP address, etc..)\n2. Distribution: signedURL distributed to authorized user, \n3. Validation: check signRUL< verify public key, timestamp expiration and other restriction",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** Large file upload handle\n-- call use techique like chunking to break file into smaller pieces and upload independently\n-- chunking happen in client before it send to server\n-- user resume upload, we could check chunks field to see which chunk has been upload and which hasn't\n-- to keep chunks field in sync:\n---> can implement server-side verification of chunk uploads using ETags.\n---> can leverage S3 multipart upload\n--> verify these ETags by calling S3's ListParts API, \nproviding an efficient way to validate multiple chunks at once. \n\n--  Content-Defined Chunking (CDC), where chunk boundaries are determined by the file's content \nusing a rolling hash (like Rabin fingerprinting). With CDC, \na small edit only affects the chunks immediately surrounding the change, \nthe vast majority of chunks remain identical. \nThis is how systems like Dropbox actually achieve efficient delta sync in practice.\n-- Also can utilize compression to speed up upload/download. compression is only useful\nif speed gained from transferring fewer bytes outweight time it take to compress\nand decompress the file\n\n** Ensure file security\n-- ensure file are secure and only accessible to authorized users\n1. Generation: signURL on server, include URL path, expiration timestamp,\nrestriction (IP address, etc..)\n2. Distribution: signedURL distributed to authorized user, \n3. Validation: check signRUL< verify public key, timestamp expiration and other restriction",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "fc7EpdjfFGZAPvsVWGU2d",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -63.80315988711175,
      "y": 1798.134485467716,
      "width": 283.13983154296875,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0F",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 560515214,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 787157219,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782162506688,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "{\n  \"id\": \"123\",\n  \"name\": \"file.txt\",\n  \"size\": 1000,\n  \"mimeType\": \"text/plain\",\n  \"uploadedBy\": \"user1\",\n  \"status\": \"uploading\",\n  \"chunks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"chunk1\",\n      \"status\": \"uploaded\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"chunk2\",\n      \"status\": \"uploading\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"chunk3\",\n      \"status\": \"not-uploaded\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "{\n  \"id\": \"123\",\n  \"name\": \"file.txt\",\n  \"size\": 1000,\n  \"mimeType\": \"text/plain\",\n  \"uploadedBy\": \"user1\",\n  \"status\": \"uploading\",\n  \"chunks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"chunk1\",\n      \"status\": \"uploaded\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"chunk2\",\n      \"status\": \"uploading\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"chunk3\",\n      \"status\": \"not-uploaded\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
